Z||000030||TRiAD||10-23-2001||11:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroKyle:<BR><B>...Forumla 1 vs NASCAR, uh I believe that is apples and oranges. I will stick to my stock racing. They can rub and race without have a wheel fly off the car with a tap. But thats my opinion...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nascar has low-pressure tires and soft suspensions, and full bodies. <BR>F1 has high-pressure tires, nearly NO suspension travel, and simply an extension of the carbon-fiber tub wrapped around the components. <BR>You're right, apples to oranges...but you're wrong on which is which. The F1 driver is certainly more "on the edge" than a Nascar driver will ever be, simply by the design of the car, and the geometry of the suspension. <BR>Watch an F1 race sometime...closely. Watch the drivers' inputs and the cars' reactions. <BR>Nascar is like driving big Buicks or Caddys, and F1 is like driving giant Carts. No comparison. <P>||||reg||1
